<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="8b90e8bc">&lt;p&gt;
    The scope, approach and supporting details become inputs to the prospective timeline. This work needs to be sequenced
    in an order that will allow the project team to meet the project’s objectives. Arranging the work requires
    practitioners to consider many factors, such as:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        What order of execution of activities is necessary to reach the objective?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        What are the required start or end dates?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        What are the scheduling dependencies?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        How is the resource plan affected by the timeline?
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Defining the overall project timeline requires consideration of the relationships between the activities and their
    time-based dependencies. This process, often termed scheduling, organizes the activities into a logical order after
    considering:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Desired start and finish dates (duration)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Work (level of effort)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Dependencies such as:
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li style=&quot;LIST-STYLE-TYPE: none&quot;&gt;
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Finish-to-start precedence (one activity must finish before another starts)
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Start-to-start precedence (two tasks must commence at the same time)
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Concurrency of activities and tasks
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Utilization of resources (e.g., full vs. part time resources, length of standard work week)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Slack time (periods where there is flexibility in starting or finishing work)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Non-working time (holidays or pre-planned breaks)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Flexibility in any of the above
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    These general scheduling concerns can be addressed through additional planning of the project activities.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
